{"tool_name":"metlin","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"metlin","home":"https://metlin.scripps.edu/","license":"Not licensed","summary":"Metabolite mass spectrometry database with multiple searching capabilities, including precursor ion, neutral loss, accurate mass, and product ions.","addition_date":"2024-08-12T15:43:14.793586Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T13:49:34.980621Z","tool_type":["Database portal"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:metlin","edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Compound ID (KEGG)","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2605"},"format":[{"term":"Textual format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2330"}]},{"data":{"term":"Molecular mass","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_0844"},"format":[{"term":"Textual format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2330"}]}],"operation":[{"term":"Database search","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2421"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"Molecule identifier","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_0982"},"format":[{"term":"Textual format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2330"}]},{"data":{"term":"Small molecule structure","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_1463"},"format":[{"term":"PNG","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3603"}]}]}],"maturity":"Mature","name":"METLIN","owner":"n.m.palmblad@lumc.nl","publication":[{"doi":"10.1097/01.ftd.0000179845.53213.39","metadata":{"abstract":"Endogenous metabolites have gained increasing interest over the past 5 years largely for their implications in diagnostic and pharmaceutical biomarker discovery. METLIN (http://metlin.scripps.edu), a freely accessible web-based data repository, has been developed to assist in a broad array of metabolite research and to facilitate metabolite identification through mass analysis. METLIN includes an annotated list of known metabolite structural information that is easily cross-correlated with its catalogue of high-resolution Fourier transform mass spe